Declare the three requant tables extern, so each is defined once.

requant.h states them at file scope with no `extern`, which in C is a
tentative definition: both translation units that include it -- requant.c and
mpc_decoder.c -- get one, and requant.c also has the real initialised
definitions. Before GCC 10 the default -fcommon merged them; since -fno-common
became the default it is a link error:

  ld: multiple definition of `Res_bit'; requant.c.o: first defined here

Cog does not carry this fix because it builds the library for macOS alone,
where it happens to link. -fcommon would also silence it and is the wrong
answer: the declarations are meant to be declarations.

--- a/libmpcdec/requant.h
+++ b/libmpcdec/requant.h
@@ -47,9 +47,9 @@
 
 
 /* C O N S T A N T S */
-const mpc_uint8_t      Res_bit [18];     ///< Bits per sample for chosen quantizer
-const MPC_SAMPLE_FORMAT __Cc    [1 + 18]; ///< Requantization coefficients
-const mpc_int16_t       __Dc    [1 + 18]; ///< Requantization offset
+extern const mpc_uint8_t      Res_bit [18];     ///< Bits per sample for chosen quantizer
+extern const MPC_SAMPLE_FORMAT __Cc    [1 + 18]; ///< Requantization coefficients
+extern const mpc_int16_t       __Dc    [1 + 18]; ///< Requantization offset
 
 #define Cc (__Cc + 1)
 #define Dc (__Dc + 1)
